workflows:
initialization_environment_check:
trigger: After `if_memory_bank_exists` completes successfully.
steps: - Check `productContext.md` content for the "## Development Environment & Engine" section and its fields. - If any key field (Engine Name, Engine Version, Language, Platform, VCS) is missing or placeholder: - Use `ask_followup_question` tool. - question: "Before we proceed, please provide the core technical details for this project: What is the Game Engine & Version, Primary Programming Language(s), Target Platform(s), and Version Control System?" - follow_up: (Provide examples like Godot 4.2/GDScript/PC/Git, Unity 2022.3/C#/Mobile/Perforce) - On response: Use `apply_diff` to update the "## Development Environment & Engine" section in `productContext.md`. - If complete: Proceed.
task_validation:
trigger: Receiving handoff from Code/Test indicating task completion requiring validation.
steps: - Review context provided (user feedback, test results, link to task/issue). - Read relevant sections of `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`, `issuesLog.md`. - Make validation decision (Pass/Fail). - If Fail: - Increment `Consecutive Failed Attempts` in `activeContext.md` using `apply_diff`. - Check if failure count >= 3. - If Yes: Trigger `failure_loop_escalation` workflow internally. - If No: Provide feedback, hand back to Code/Debug mode. - If Pass: - Update `progress.md` (mark task complete). - Update `issuesLog.md` (set status to Resolved/Closed, add validation note) if applicable. - Reset `Consecutive Failed Attempts` in `activeContext.md` to 0 using `apply_diff`. - Inform user of successful validation.
architectural_review:
trigger: Receiving handoff from Code/Debug due to `architectural_review_needed`.
steps: - Acknowledge review request. - Analyze proposed change (diff) and context. - Compare against `productContext.md`, `decisionLog.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `progress.md`. - Determine if change is significant and unplanned. - If Minor/Planned: Approve, document if needed (`decisionLog.md`), hand back to original mode to proceed. - If Significant/Unplanned: - Analyze and document implications. - Use `ask_followup_question` to consult user about the deviation and implications. - If user approves: Document decision in `decisionLog.md`, update `productContext.md` if needed, hand back to original mode to proceed. - If user rejects/discusses: Work with original mode/user to find alternative, update `activeContext.md`.
failure_loop_escalation:
trigger: Receiving handoff from Code/Debug due to `recurring_failure_escalation` OR internal trigger from `task_validation` workflow when threshold is met.
steps: - Acknowledge escalation. - Review context (`activeContext.md` failure count, history, logs). - Decide next strategic step: - Option A: Request web search via Ask mode (for docs/solutions). Formulate query, hand off. - Option B: Request deeper debugging via Debug mode. Hand off. - Option C: Re-evaluate strategy/requirements with User via `ask_followup_question`. - Option D: Log formally in `issuesLog.md` if not already done. - Instruct the next mode/step. - Reset `Consecutive Failed Attempts` in `activeContext.md` to 0 _only if_ providing fundamentally new guidance based on analysis (e.g., after Ask returns web results).
